; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3747  ** Traceability: [cover parentID={E7F3E2D7-36B5-4165-BEC5-C847DAEE25C3},
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3748                                   {BA6EFE0D-B9E6-4630-BF56-93FFA7D4CB7F}]      **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3749  **                                                                            **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3750  ** Syntax           : Std_ReturnType Adc_SetPowerState                        **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3751  **                    (                                                       **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3752  **                      Adc_PowerStateRequestResultType * const Result        **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3753  **                    )                                                       **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3754  **                                                                            **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3755  ** Description      : API configures the ADC module so that it enters the     **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3756  **                    already prepared power state,chosen between a predefined**
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3757  **                    set of configured ones.The API must be invoked from all **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3758  **                    the cores using the ADC driver, as each call sets the   **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3759  **                    power state only for the ADC hardware groups used by    **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3760  **                    the calling core                                        **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3761  **             Note: 1.When the converter is set to 'full power mode', then   **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3762  **                     the conversion is started immediately by the hardware  **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3763  **                     after a request (no additional time delay). This is the**
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3764  **                     default mode after modules initialization.             **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3765  **                   2.When the converter is set to 'Fast standby mode' or    **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3766  **                     'Slow standby mode' and no conversion is requested,then**
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3767  **                     it saves power. When a conversion is triggered then the**
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3768  **                     converter wakes up automatically, but it needs certain **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3769  **                     wake-up time before conversions can be performed. There**
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3770  **                     is no power saving while the conversions are being     **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3771  **                     performed during this mode.During this phase the driver**
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3772  **                     reports the current power state as 'Fast standby mode' **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3773  **                     or 'Slow standby mode'. In this mode, when the         **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3774  **                     conversion is no longer active,then the converter saves**
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3775  **                     power and a new conversion request will trigger the    **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3776  **                     wake-up cycle again (time delay for wake-up).          **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3777  **                   3.When the converter is set to 'off mode',it enters power**
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3778  **                     saving mode and no further conversions are possible    **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3779  **                     until a power mode transition is made explicitly to    **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3780  **                     come out of 'off mode'.                                **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3781  **                   4.This API is available only when                        **
; ..\MCAL364\Adc\ssc\src\Adc.c	  3782  **                     AdcLowPowerStatesSupport is configured as true.        **
